WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.210
The Qur'an sets a fixed
punishment for theft.

2
00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:06.570
On the page, it reads
like an absolute rule.

3
00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:10.350
Yet around the year 639,
in a time of famine,

4
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.910
the Caliph Umar is reported
to have suspended it.

5
00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:17.290
Western philosophy offers
three boxes for ethics:

6
00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:20.110
duty, results and character.

7
00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:24.140
So is Muslim ethics about
rules, results or character,

8
00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.080
or all three at once?

9
00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:29.190
In this mission, you'll
meet an old Muslim debate:

10
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:34.190
is an act good because God commands
it, or commanded because it is good?

11
00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:38.780
Then you'll set the purposes of Islamic
law beside Bentham's calculus of pleasure

12
00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:40.040
and pain.

13
00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:43.780
Your mission: weigh up whether
Muslim ethics is about rules,

14
00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:46.520
results, character, or all three.
